---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Life Insurance Needs Calculator (DIME Method)" description="Calculate exactly how much life insurance coverage your family needs using the DIME method.">
  <main class="container">
    <h1>Life Insurance Needs Calculator</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Find out how much coverage your family needs using the DIME method.</p>

    <div class="calc-box">
      <div class="input-group"><label>Total Debts (Credit Cards, Car Loans) ($)</label><input type="number" id="debts" placeholder="e.g. 15000" /></div>
      <div class="input-group"><label>Annual Income to Replace ($)</label><input type="number" id="income" placeholder="e.g. 60000" /></div>
      <div class="input-group"><label>Remaining Mortgage Balance ($)</label><input type="number" id="mortgage" placeholder="e.g. 250000" /></div>
      <div class="input-group"><label>Estimated Education Costs ($)</label><input type="number" id="education" placeholder="e.g. 100000" /></div>
      <button id="calcBtn">Calculate Coverage</button>
      <div id="result" class="hidden result-box">
        <p class="total">Recommended Coverage: <strong id="coverage"></strong></p>
        <p class="sub">Breakdown: <span>Debt + 10x Income + Mortgage + Education</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="article-content">
      <h2>What is the DIME Method?</h2>
      <p>The DIME method is a simple, highly effective way to calculate your life insurance needs. It stands for <strong>D</strong>ebt, <strong>I</strong>ncome, <strong>M</strong>ortgage, and <strong>E</strong>ducation.</p>
      <p>By adding your total debts, 10 years of your income, your remaining mortgage balance, and estimated future education costs for your children, you get a very accurate picture of the financial safety net your family needs.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  document.getElementById('calcBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const d = parseFloat(document.getElementById('debts').value) || 0;
    const i = parseFloat(document.getElementById('income').value) || 0;
    const m = parseFloat(document.getElementById('mortgage').value) || 0;
    const e = parseFloat(document.getElementById('education').value) || 0;

    if (d === 0 && i === 0 && m === 0 && e === 0) { alert("Please enter at least one value."); return; }

    // DIME Method Math
    const totalCoverage = d + (i * 10) + m + e;

    document.getElementById('coverage').innerText = "$" + totalCoverage.toLocaleString('en-US', {minimumFractionDigits: 2});
    document.getElementById('result').classList.remove('hidden');
  });
</script>

<style>
  .container { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px; }
  h1 { text-align: center; } .subtitle { text-align: center; color: #6b7280; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .calc-box { background: white; padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); max-width: 400px; margin: 32px auto; }
  .input-group { margin-bottom: 16px; } .input-group label { display: block; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .input-group input { width: 100%; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 4px; box-sizing: border-box; }
  button { width: 100%; padding: 10px; background: #2563eb; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; }
  .result-box { margin-top: 24px; padding: 16px; background: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 4px; }
  .hidden { display: none; } .total { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; } .sub { font-size: 14px; color: #4b5563; }
  .article-content { margin-top: 40px; line-height: 1.6; } .article-content h2 { margin-top: 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding-bottom: 8px; }
</style>
